  "raw": {
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Information-Literacy-and-First-Year-Engagement-Librarian---Assistant-Professor--Professor-of-Practice_R-002186": {
      "title": "Information Literacy and First-Year Engagement Librarian,  Assistant Librarian - Professional Practice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Library Faculty Job Summary The Librarian will provide instruction as well as assess and refine the library’s information literacy program to ensure that it meets the needs of the campus. This position will support AI literacy as well as ensure that students have the digital literacy skills needed to be adept at using campus technology and productivity software. S/he will collaborate with library and other campus faculty/partners to design and create active learning environments both in the classroom and online. This position will lead the library’s efforts in first year student outreach and engagement. Job Description RESPONSIBILITIES: Assess and grow the library’s information literacy instruction program. Develop and deliver instruction that effectively and ethically promotes information, digital, and AI literacy. Work collaboratively with other university partners, including the First-Year Writing Program, University Success Program, and the Center for Teaching Innovation to design and deliver classroom and web-based instruction for first year students to develop a basic level of information literacy. Develop instructional materials and e-learning modules to support the online learning environment. Provide support and professional development for other librarians and staff involved in instruction, including workshops on improving teaching effectiveness and incorporating AI and other technologies that impact student learning. Evaluate library instruction activities and compile, analyze, and report relevant statistics. Create assessment strategies to measure the success of information literacy instruction sessions. Represent the library at student recruiting events held throughout the year. Present library programs to new students at MAMBO, Privateer Plunge, and Spring Splash. Provide reference and research consultation services including on call hours, chat and email coverage. Provide specialized instruction and research assistance/consultation services in assigned subject areas. Promote digital literacy training opportunities to the campus and New Orleans community, particularly in the Gentilly neighborhood near the UNO campus. Required Qualifications: MLS or equivalent degree from an American Library Association accredited program or international equivalent. Demonstrated teaching ability. Expertise in threshold concepts and the information literacy framework. Web design and instructional technology skills. Proficiency in the use of computer applications for teaching and learning. Expertise with standard office software including word processing and spreadsheets. Ability to adapt to rapidly changing technologies and environments. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, both orally and in writing. Ability to work independently and in a team-oriented environment. A commitment to professional service and scholarship. Desired Qualifications: Two years of instruction experience in an academic library. Instructional design background. Experience with assessment of student learning. Experience in developing and teaching for-credit information literacy courses at the university level. Experience using LibGuides to create instructional resources Interest in integrating new “makerspace” resources and services into the instruction curriculum. Experience with course management software (Canvas). Participant in ACRL Information Literacy Immersion Program. Subject specialist and collection development experience particularly in the sciences and engineering. Required Attachments Please upload the following documents in the Resume/Cover Letter section.  Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and LSU New Orleans; Names and contact information of three references; Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor--Educational-Administration_R-002067": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Educational Administration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Educational Leadership, Counseling and Foundations Job Summary Job Description School of Education / Education al Administration Program     Assistant Professor of Education (tenure-track)       Job Description      The School of Education at the LSU New Orleans invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Educational Administration with a b ackground in Higher Education Administration or K12 Educational Administration . The successful candidate will have an excellent track record of K12 or post-secondary teaching , a preference for collaborative work, a strong commitment to urban institutions , and an established or emerging research agenda in an area of Educational Ad m inistration .      This position is responsible for 9 academic units per semester ( 3 / 3 ).       Responsibilities include teaching Masters and Doctoral-level courses in E ducation al Administration , s ervice to the department/college, community, and the profession, and scholarly productivity in an area of e ducational a dministration /leadership , e ducational change, educational policy, or urban education .  Other responsibilities include supervision of doctoral student research , student recruitment and advising , pursuit of extra-mural research funding, community outreach , and other support s to the administrative functions of the unit.      How to Apply      Please submit :   (1) a curriculum vitae    (2) a letter of interest in the position, noting achievements in teaching and scholar s hip     (3) a published ( or in preparation ) example of your scholarly work (article or chapter)     (4) a one-page teaching philosophy statement   (5) a one-page research agenda overview, and     (5) the names and contact information for three references.      Application materials should be submitted to the Director of the School of Education , Dr. Brian Beabout , by October 30 th . While we will begin reviewing and scheduling interviews at that time, the position will remain open until filled, and applications will be considered after the deadline if a preferred candidate is not identified in the first round of submissions.      Required Qualifications    · Ph.D. or other terminal degree in Educational Administration or related field.   · Evidence of an emerging research agenda .   · Evidence/potential for excellence in teaching and mentorship   · Evidence/potential for service to the university , community , and profession         Desired Qualifications    · Evidence of teaching excellence at the K12 or Postsecondary level ( both on-campus and online ) .   · Demonstrable expertise in teaching students from diverse backgrounds .   · Leadership experience in a K12 or Postsecondary setting     Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
