    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Associate-Professor--Power-and-Energy-Systems_R-002185": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Power and Energy Systems",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Electrical Engineering Job Summary Job Description The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at the LSU New Orleans invites applications for a tenured Associate Professor position in Power and Energy Systems , beginning Fall 2027. About New Orleans and LSU New Orleans New Orleans is one of the most distinctive cities in the United States, known for its rich cultural heritage, music, cuisine, and historic architecture. It is the largest city in Louisiana, a major U.S. port, and a regional hub for tourism, healthcare, education, and the energy sector. The city’s expanding industries in energy, advanced manufacturing, maritime commerce, and technology create strong opportunities for university–industry collaboration. The LSU New Orleans ranks #261 of 2,496 U.S. universities (~top 10%) and #986 of 14,131 globally (~top 7%), placing it #3 in Louisiana according to EduRank. The LSU New Orleans, Dr. Robert A. Savoie College of Engineering ranks #3 in Louisiana and #202 of 2,454 U.S. engineering programs (~top 8%), with EduRank identifying LSU New Orleans as performing in the top 50% across engineering‑related topics. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) ranks #4 in Louisiana and #200 of 2,454 U.S. electrical engineering programs (~top 8%), reflecting strong regional and national standing. LSU New Orleans is home to the Power and Energy Research Laboratory (PERL) , established in 2009, which serves as a regional hub for advanced power and energy research. PERL maintains strong ties to local industry, utilities, and regional partners, providing rich opportunities for collaboration, applied research, and technology transfer. Recent research areas at PERL include: 1. Integration of renewable energy (solar and wind) into the electric grid, 2. Inverter‑based resources protection, 3. Stability, resiliency, reliability, and security studies for modern power systems, 4. Hardware‑in‑the‑loop real‑time modeling and simulation Position Responsibilities Maintain a high‑impact, externally funded research program in power and energy systems Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in electrical engineering, particularly in power and energy Supervise graduate students and mentor undergraduate researchers Engage in collaborative research with PERL and regional industry partners Contribute to curriculum development, accreditation activities, and departmental service Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in Electrical Engineering Expertise in power electronics, renewable energy systems, application of artificial intelligence and machine learning in power systems, or a closely related area Prior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor (or equivalent) at an accredited academic institution Evidence of a strong research record, including peer‑reviewed publications Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level Desired Qualifications Experience securing competitive research funding Industry collaboration or technology‑transfer experience Experience with real‑time simulation platforms or hardware‑in‑the‑loop systems Commitment to inclusive excellence and student success Applicants should submit: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement Contact information for three references Review of applications will begin in October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Associate-Professor-Public-Administration---Master-of-Public-Administration-Coordinator_R-002168": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor Public Administration & Master of Public Administration Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Political Science Job Summary Job Description The Department of Political Science invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Public Administration in the Division of Planning and Public Affairs for spring or fall 2027. We seek an innovative teacher-scholar with expertise in public administration, public policy, nonprofit management, emergency management, public finance, or a related field. Area of specialization is open. The successful candidate will teach graduate courses in our NASPAA-accredited Master of Public Administration (MPA) program and serve as the MPA Program Coordinator , providing leadership for curriculum development, assessment, student recruitment and advising, accreditation activities, and continuous program improvement. They will also be expected to develop and sustain an active, nationally recognized research agenda with the potential to secure external funding. Faculty in the Division of Planning and Public Affairs are encouraged to pursue interdisciplinary research and collaborate with the Division's research centers, including the Center for Hazards Assessment, Response, and Technology (CHART) and the LSU New Orleans Transportation Institute (UNOTI) . This position is responsible for 9 academic units per semester (3/3) for faculty who maintain an active research agenda. Course releases may be given for robust funded research activities or extensive service responsibilities as appropriate.  Responsibilities include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, and supervising master and doctoral students in Public Affairs, Political Science, and Urban Studies, as well as other courses that are within the candidate’s area of expertise. We welcome applicants whose scholarship addresses contemporary policy challenges and who are committed to advancing the urban mission of a growing planning and public affairs division through excellence in research, teaching, and professional engagement. How to Apply Please submit: (1) a curriculum vitae (2) a letter of interest in the position, noting achievements in publishing, and teaching (3) a one-page teaching philosophy, and (4) the names and contact information for three references. Application materials should be submitted via the University’s application system, Attn: Chair, Dr. Marla Nelson.  Application review will begin on October 19 2026.  For full consideration, applications should be received by 11:59 PM on October 18, 2026.    While we will begin reviewing and scheduling interviews at that time, the position will remain open until filled. Required Qualifications   A Ph.D. in Public Administration, Political Science, or a closely related field or be ABD with a clear date of completion. For Associate Professor consideration, prior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor (or equivalent) at an accredited academic institution Preferred Qualifications   Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels in both online teaching as well as in the traditional classroom settings. Evidence of an active or emerging research agenda with the potential for external funding and publication in peer-reviewed journals. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Professional-Practice--Clinical-Practicum---Internship-Coordinator--Counselor-Education_R-002087": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice, Clinical Practicum & Internship Coordinator, Counselor Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Educational Leadership, Counseling and Foundations Job Summary Job Description The Counselor Education Program within the LSU New Orleans School of Education seeks applicants for a non-tenure track full-time Assistant Professor of Professional Practice, which is equivalent to a clinical faculty position. The Assistant Professor of Professional Practice will also serve as the Clinical Practicum & Internship Coordinator for the CACREP accredited graduate programs in counseling: M.Ed. in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, M.Ed. in School Counseling, and Ph.D. in Counselor Education. The successful candidate will have established teaching, clinical, and supervision philosophies, a preference for collaborative work, a strong commitment to mentoring counseling students, and established clinical experience. This is an in-person position that is responsible for 12 academic units per semester (4/4 – with the expectation of a release for administrative responsibilities associated with the Clinical Practicum & Internship Coordinator position) Example of Duties: Serving as the Clinical Practicum & Internship coordinator for the program; responsible for the coordination of practicum and internship experiences in Clinical Mental Health and School Counseling masters programs and the doctoral program in Counselor Education Responding to inquiries regarding practicum and internship Supervising doctoral supervisors as they supervise master's students On-going connection with and monitoring of field experience sites for practicum and internship students. Developing and fostering new sites for practicum and internship students Advising students through the clinical phase of the program Onboarding students, sites, liaisons, and University Supervisors Coordinating Supervision Assist, the program’s electronic field experience and supervision management software Overseeing completion of field experience paperwork and documentation and confirming student liability insurance coverage Teaching graduate courses within the Counselor Education Program Student advising How to Apply: Please submit: A current curriculum vitae A letter of interest in the position, noting achievements in teaching and clinical experience A one-page philosophy statement for each: teaching, supervision, and counseling practice The names and contact information for three professional references, at least one of which can speak directly to applicant’s teaching skills  Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered  Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in counseling or counselor education from a CACREP accredited institution of higher education to meet CACREP core faculty standards (ABD may be considered for candidates in final stages of their dissertation) Eligibility for Louisiana state licensure as a Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) and/or certification as a School Counselor Desired Qualifications Preparation and experience in clinical supervision Specialized counseling experience in clinical mental health and/or school counseling Experience in supervising counselors in training Experience in working with practicum and internship students and/or sites Evidence of teaching excellence at the University level Demonstrable expertise in teaching students from diverse backgrounds and with diverse academic and developmental needs Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Commitment to the preparation of counselors Commitment to effective, ethical, and multicultural competent graduate teaching and supervision Demonstrated effective interpersonal skills and collegiality. Posting Close Date: This position will remain open until filled.  This is for an August 2027 start date (with the potential for January 2027 if all parties agree) Note to Applicant:  Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their letter of interest. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.  References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.  This position will require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate selected for hire.  As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at the LSU-New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.  Any questions regarding the position can be directed towards the Program Chair, Dr. Michelle E. Wade at mewade@lsuneworleans.edu  However, all applications and materials MUST be submitted through the university's career portal ( Careers at LSU New Orleans | LSU New Orleans ) Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
