    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor--Economics-and-Finance_R-002088": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Economics and Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Economics and Finance Job Summary Job Description ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF FINANCE Tenure-Track LSU New Orleans is a welcoming university in one of America’s most vibrant cities. Is This The Right Job For You? This position is a great opportunity to join a department with a long and strong history of serving the economics profession needs in New Orleans and beyond.  The Department offers the BS and MS in Finance as well as a PhD in Financial Economics. We have successfully placed more than 150 PhD graduates into universities across the United States and the world as well as many into industry. These graduates have been very successful in publishing and thus gaining tenure at their respective universities. LSU New Orleans Finance students mirror the local community and also come from across the globe.  You will enjoy a city with unmatched history, culture, and character.  If you want to learn more, these quotes by well-known authors are a great place to start - https://www.goodreads.com/quotes/tag/new-orleans . Job Summary Teach four finance classes per 9-month academic year (2-2 load) at the undergraduate and graduate levels.  Our greatest need is to teach courses in International Finance including a PhD Seminar and a PhD Seminar in Econometrics so a strong preference will be given to applicants with those competencies and with demonstrated teaching skills. Publish research suitable for acceptance in leading finance journals. Perform appropriate service activities for the university as well as the local and professional communities. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Finance or Economics completed by August 2027. Evidence of ability to publish in academic journals. Good verbal and written communication skills. Application Requirements A complete application requires the following materials: Detailed curriculum vitae or resume; Cover letter; Three letters of recommendation. Application Deadline For full consideration, all application materials should be submitted through the LSU New Orleans employment portal by 11:59 p.m. (Central Time) on September 30, 2026 . Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Professional-Practice---Healthcare-Management_R-002089": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice - Healthcare Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Management and Marketing Job Summary The Henry Bernstein College of Business Administration at LSU New Orleans invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Professional Practice in Healthcare Management. The position serves the AUPHA-certified Bachelor of Science in Healthcare Management within the AACSB-accredited Henry Bernstein College of Business Administration. The program prepares future healthcare leaders through applied study of healthcare delivery, leadership, operations, finance and revenue cycle management, quality improvement, population health, long-term services and supports, and health information systems. LSU New Orleans seeks a healthcare practitioner-educator with director-level or higher leadership experience in healthcare delivery. The strongest candidates will bring substantial expertise in one or more of the following priority areas: long-term services and supports/long-term care (LTSS/LTC); healthcare finance, accounting, reimbursement, or revenue cycle and collections; public or population health; or health information systems, informatics, and digital health. The position primarily supports the undergraduate Healthcare Management program, develops applied learning and employer partnerships, and contributes to the program's growth and professional relevance. Job Description Assistant Professor of Professional Practice – Healthcare Management Department of Management & Marketing Henry Bernstein College of Business Administration Job Summary The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach a regular course load of four courses per semester , primarily undergraduate healthcare management courses during the Fall and Spring semesters. Teach in face-to-face, hybrid, synchronous online, and asynchronous online instructional formats as assigned. Teach within the Healthcare Management curriculum, with priority coverage in LTSS/LTC; healthcare finance, accounting, reimbursement, and revenue cycle; public and population health; or health information systems and informatics. Translate current healthcare leadership practice, regulation, technology, and evidence into applied undergraduate learning. Mentor undergraduate students regarding academic planning, internships, graduate education, and professional career development. Support internship, practicum, and capstone experiences through engagement with healthcare employers and community partners. Submit course assessment reports, Assurance of Learning documentation, and other accreditation-related materials in a timely manner to support AACSB and AUPHA accreditation requirements. Participate in curriculum review, continuous improvement initiatives, and student learning assessment activities. Work collaboratively with faculty and administrators to support the continued development, recruitment, retention, and growth of the Healthcare Management Program. Participate in departmental, college, university, healthcare-industry, and professional service activities appropriate to an Assistant Professor of Professional Practice appointment. Maintain active professional engagement in healthcare leadership through executive practice, healthcare consulting, professional education, applied scholarship, or leadership in healthcare associations, consistent with AACSB faculty qualification standards. Required Qualifications Earned terminal degree from an accredited institution in a healthcare-focused discipline. Qualifying degrees include a Doctor of Health Science or Sciences (DHS/DHSc), Doctor of Health Administration (DHA), Doctor of Healthcare Leadership (DHL), Doctor of Public Health (DrPH), an EdD in Leadership or Organizational Leadership with a documented healthcare focus, or a research doctorate in healthcare management, health administration, health services, public/population health, health informatics, or a closely related healthcare field. The degree must be completed by the appointment date. Senior healthcare leadership experience : at least five (5) years of progressively responsible, full-time professional experience in healthcare, including service at the Director, executive, or equivalent senior leadership level with responsibility for people, budgets, programs, systems, or organizational outcomes. Demonstrated depth in at least one priority domain : LTSS/LTC; healthcare finance, accounting, reimbursement, or revenue cycle and collections; public or population health; or health information systems, informatics, and digital health. Applicants must also demonstrate: Ability to translate senior-level healthcare experience into applied, evidence-based undergraduate instruction. Commitment to excellence in undergraduate healthcare management education. Ability to effectively teach and mentor a diverse student population. Ability to interpret healthcare data, evaluate operational and population-health challenges, establish priorities, and communicate decisions clearly. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and external healthcare partners. Desired Qualifications University teaching experience in healthcare management, health administration, health services, public health, health informatics, or a closely related healthcare discipline. Experience teaching in online, hybrid, and technology-enhanced learning environments. Director-level or higher responsibility across more than one healthcare setting or priority domain. Experience leading measurable improvement in healthcare financial performance, revenue realization, access, quality, population outcomes, LTSS/LTC operations, or health information-system implementation. Experience supervising student internships or experiential learning. Evidence of healthcare-focused applied scholarship, consulting, professional education, or executive development. Healthcare-specific professional certification or licensure, such as: Fellow of the American College of Healthcare Executives (FACHE) HFMA Certified Healthcare Financial Professional (CHFP) or Certified Revenue Cycle Representative (CRCR) Certified in Public Health (CPH) Certified Professional in Healthcare Information and Management Systems (CPHIMS), Certified Associate in Healthcare Information and Management Systems (CAHIMS), or Registered Health Information Administrator (RHIA) Licensed Nursing Home Administrator (LNHA/NHA) or a comparable LTSS/LTC credential Certified Professional in Healthcare Quality (CPHQ) or another healthcare-specific leadership credential Active participation in healthcare organizations such as ACHE, AUPHA, HFMA, ACHCA, HIMSS, AHIMA, APHA, LeadingAge, or related professional associations. Application Requirements A complete application requires the following materials: Detailed curriculum vitae or resume documenting the terminal degree, Director-level or higher healthcare positions, scope of responsibility, measurable accomplishments in the priority field(s), teaching experience, certifications, and healthcare-focused scholarly or professional activity. Cover letter identifying the applicant's primary priority domain and explaining how the applicant's senior healthcare leadership experience will strengthen LSU New Orleans and the Healthcare Management Program. Statement of teaching philosophy. Names and complete contact information for three professional references . Unofficial transcripts for all earned degrees. Finalists may be asked to provide: Official transcripts. Evidence of teaching effectiveness. Professional presentation or teaching demonstration. Application Deadline For full consideration, all application materials should be submitted through the LSU New Orleans employment portal by 11:59 p.m. (Central Time) on September 30, 2026 . Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Appointment This is a full-time, non-tenure-track Assistant Professor of Professional Practice appointment with an anticipated start date of January 2027 (or as negotiated). Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. LSU New Orleans offers a comprehensive benefits package, including retirement, health insurance, and professional development opportunities. About the Henry Bernstein College of Business Administration The Healthcare Management Program is the only AUPHA-certified undergraduate healthcare management program in Louisiana and is housed within the AACSB-accredited Henry Bernstein College of Business Administration. The program provides nationally recognized, applied preparation for careers in healthcare leadership and administration. Faculty benefit from strong partnerships with leading healthcare organizations throughout the Greater New Orleans region and enjoy opportunities to engage in experiential education, workforce development, applied scholarship, executive education, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Professional-Practice--School-of-Interdisciplinary-Studies_R-002083": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice, School of Interdisciplinary Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department School of Interdisciplinary Studies Job Summary Job Description The School of Interdisciplinary Studies seeks to hire a Professor of Professional Practice for the Spring 2027 academic year. This full-time position will teach a regular (4/4) course load of four courses in both the Fall and Spring terms in the Interdisciplinary Studies program. In addition to instruction, the position will create and submit assessment reports and other timely administrative tasks needed for SACS accreditation; work collaboratively with LSU Online on program and course development; and support the continued development of the interdisciplinary studies program. These duties may include outreach efforts to recruit students and work with other departments across the university to develop additional interdisciplinary programs, with a focus on program growth and opportunity expansion.    Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or other terminal degree in a related field. This can include Education, Curriculum and Instruction, a Liberal Arts program, or General Business  Credentials to teach undergraduate and graduate courses that may be considered part of interdisciplinary studies. Effective communication, organization, and administrative skills Ability to multitask, collect information, analyze data, define challenges, set priorities, and draw valid conclusions in a timely manner. Desired Qualifications: Teaching experience in higher education. Curriculum design and credit evaluation. Developing methods of recognizing and accounting for non-traditional college credit.  Teaching experience in remote modality, including preparation of course content for asynchronous instructional delivery. All of the required materials must be received for an application to be considered complete. A complete application requires: ​ Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and LSU New Orleans; Names and contact information of three references; The deadline for applying is September 15, 2026, and the review will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all required materials should be submitted in the University's application portal by 11:59 PM on September 14, 2026. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
