    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor--Creative-Writing--Poetry-_R-002084": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Creative Writing (Poetry)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Language and Literature Job Summary Job Description Job Description The Department of Language and Literature at LSU New Orleans invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Creative Writing with an expertise in Poetry (at least one book published or under contact). A secondary expertise in Creative Non-Fiction is also highly desirable. This position is responsible for 12 academic units per semester (4/4). The typical teaching load is 9 units per semester (3/3), with the expectation of service (with Bayou magazine), research, and thesis mentoring to fulfill the remaining 3 units. Responsibilities include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in poetry, as well as other courses offered by the Department of Language and Literature based on need. This position will be heavily involved with the Creative Writing Workshop, the nationally renowned MFA program at LSU New Orleans, which offers both resident and online MFA programs. The successful candidate should be adept at teaching in both in-person and asynchronous modalities and have a deep investment in mentoring students through thesis projects. An ability to work with our literary magazine Bayou , as well as an eagerness to participate in the community and service of the Department of Language and Literature and the Creative Writing Workshop is also highly desirable. How to Apply Please submit: (1) a curriculum vitae (2) a letter of interest in the position, noting achievements in publishing, teaching, and service to literary communities (3) a copy of one published (or contracted) book in .pdf format (4) a one-page teaching philosophy, and (5) the names and contact information for three references. Application review will begin on October 1, 2026 and the review will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all required materials should be submitted in the University's application portal , Attn: Chair for Language and Literature, Prof. Justin Maxwell., by 11:59 PM on September 30, 2026. Required Qualifications At least one published (or under contract) book in poetry MFA or PhD in Creative Writing in hand by date of hire (January 1, 2027) Evidence of teaching excellence Desired Qualifications ​Single-authored book of poetry with distinguished press and review coverage Publication record in both Poetry and Creative Non-Fiction Experience teaching and advising graduate students Commitment to fostering supportive literary communities Salary Information: Expected salary is approximately $59,983 . The position is dependent on budgetary approval. About t he Creative Writing Workshop at LSU-New Orleans , established in 1991, is a nationally renowned MFA program in creative writing, offering degrees in fiction, poetry, creative non-fiction and playwriting. A 3 year studio/research program, it emphasizes community and mentorship, offering training in teaching, publishing, literature, and creative writing. Its alums have published well over 150 books with national presses and have recently garnered such awards as the Pulitzer Prize in Poetry, the Dylan Thomas Prize in Fiction, and have been listed for numerous other honors, including the National Book Award.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor--Planning-and-Urban-Studies_R-002091": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Planning and Urban Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Planning and Urban Studies Job Summary Job Description The Division of Planning and Public Affairs at Louisiana State University-New Orleans invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Urban and Regional Planning for fall 2027. We seek a teacher-scholar committed to advancing the field of urban and regional planning through impactful research, innovative teaching, and engagement with diverse communities. We welcome applicants from all areas of planning, with particular interest in candidates whose teaching and research include urban design, historic preservation, housing and community development, climate adaptation and environmental planning, transportation planning, or GIS and spatial analytics. The successful candidate will teach graduate courses in our Planning Accreditation Board (PAB)-accredited Master of Urban and Regional Planning (MURP) program, contribute to curriculum development and student mentoring, and demonstrate excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. They will also be expected to develop and sustain an active, nationally recognized research agenda with the potential to secure external funding. Faculty in the Division of Planning and Public Affairs are encouraged to pursue interdisciplinary research and collaborate with the Division's research centers, including the Center for Hazards Assessment, Response, and Technology (CHART) and the LSU New Orleans Transportation Institute (UNOTI). This position is responsible for 9 academic units per semester (3/3) for faculty who maintain an active research agenda. Course releases may be given for robust funded research activities or extensive service responsibilities as appropriate. Responsibilities include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, and supervising master and doctoral students in Urban and Regional Planning, Urban Studies, and/or Transportation, as well as other courses that are within the candidate’s area of expertise. Administrative duties as assigned. We welcome applicants whose scholarship addresses contemporary planning challenges and who are committed to advancing the urban mission of a growing planning and public affairs division through excellence in research, teaching, and professional engagement. The Department of Planning and Urban Studies The Master of Urban and Regional Planning (MURP) program, established in 1974, is Louisiana’s only accredited planning program. Housed in the Department of Planning and Urban Studies (PLUS) within the Division of Planning and Public Affairs (DPPA) in the College of Liberal Arts, Education, and Human Development (COLAEHD), PLUS comprises five interrelated academic programs: the MURP, Bachelor of Science in Urban Studies and Planning, Master of Science in Transportation, Master of Science in Urban Studies, and Ph.D. in Urban Studies. PLUS is also home to the LSU New Orleans Transportation Institute (UNOTI) and the Center for Hazards Assessment, Response & Technology (CHART), which collaborate across disciplines to address critical urban challenges. Through research and community engagement, PLUS advances LSU New Orleans’s mission to enhance quality of life in the New Orleans region, the Gulf South, and beyond. How to Apply Please submit: (1) a curriculum vitae (2) a letter of interest in the position, noting achievements in publishing, and teaching (3) a one-page teaching philosophy, and (4) the names and contact information for three references. Application review will begin on October 1, 2026 and the review will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all required materials should be submitted in the University's application portal, Attn: Chair, Dr. Marla Nelson, by 11:59 PM on September 30, 2026. Required Qualifications   A Ph.D. in Urban and Regional Planning, or a closely related field or be ABD with a clear date of completion. Desired Qualifications   Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels in both online teaching as well as in the traditional classroom settings. Evidence of an active or emerging research agenda with the potential for external funding and publication in peer-reviewed journals. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Professional-Practice--Mechanical-Engineering_R-002092": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Practice, Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Mechanical Engineering Job Summary Job Description Professor of Practice in Mechanical Engineering Program   LSU New Orleans College of Engineering is seeking to fill a full-time faculty position for the Mechanical Engineering Program.   The B.S. in Mechanical Engineering is offered by the Dr. Robert A. Savoie College of Engineering at LSU New Orleans.   The Department of Mechanical Engineering currently serves approximately 300 undergraduate students. In addition to the Bachelor of Science degree, students can earn Master of Science in Engineering and a Ph.D. in Engineering and Applied Science degrees.   The professor of practice position primarily supports the undergraduate program.   Job Summary Regular course load of four courses, primarily undergraduate mechanical engineering courses, in both the Fall and Spring term. Teach courses in other engineering disciplines based on the needs of the college. Timely submission of assessment reports and other administrative tasks needed for accreditation. Work collaboratively with colleagues to support the continued development of the mechanical engineering program.   Required Qualifications Ph.D. degree in mechanical engineering or a related field; or M.S. in mechanical engineering or a related field combined with > 5 years of industry experience as a practicing engineer. Effective communication, organization, and administrative skills Ability to multi-task, collect information, analyze data, define challenges, set priorities, and draw valid conclusions in a timely manner.   Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in higher education. Teaching experience in multiple engineering disciplines. All of the required materials must be received for an application to be considered complete. A complete application requires: ​Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and LSU New Orleans; Names and contact information of three references; The deadline for applying is September 1, 2026 and the review will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all required materials should be submitted in the University's application portal by 11:59 PM on August 31, 2026. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Computer-Science_R-002040": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-22\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department Computer Science Job Summary Job Description Assistant Professor of Computer Science — LSU New Orleans The Department of Computer Science at LSU New Orleans invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning Spring 2027. The department seeks candidates whose research centers on artificial intelligence, with particular emphasis on AI for cybersecurity, bioinformatics, gaming and simulation experiences, and autonomous vehicles. Strong candidates in closely related AI areas will also be considered. About the Department: The department offers undergraduate and graduate programs, including a Ph.D. And hosts two research centers. Faculty maintains active research programs in AI, cybersecurity and digital forensics, bioinformatics, environmental informatics, gaming and simulations, and autonomous vehicles. The university is located in New Orleans, a culturally distinctive city with a growing technology and defense sector. Responsibilities: Establish and sustain an externally funded research program; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; supervise graduate students; and provide service to the department, university, and profession. To Apply: Application materials should be submitted via the University's careers portal, Attention: Dr. Md Tamjidul Hoque. A complete application must include: A cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Research statement. Teaching statement. Contact information for three references. The anticipated start date for the individual hired will be Spring 2027. All of the required materials must be received for an application to be considered complete. The deadline for applying is September 1, 2026 and the review will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all required materials should be submitted in the University's application portal by 11:59 PM on August 31, 2026. Required Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field by the appointment start date. A record of high-quality research with demonstrated potential for external funding. A commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring. Salary: Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
    },
    "https://ulsuno.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UniversityOfNewOrleans/job/New-Orleans-La/Instructor-of-Philosophy_R-002024": {
      "title": "Instructor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-21\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in LSU New Orleans. Once you start the application process, you will not be able to save your work, so you should collect all required information before you begin.  The required information is listed below in the job posting.   You must complete all required portions of the application and attach the required documents in order to be considered for employment.   Department History and Philosophy Job Summary Job Description The Philosophy Division/College of Liberal Arts, Social Inquiry, and Human Development at Louisiana State University New Orleans invites applications for a non-tenure-track Instructor position in Philosophy (4/4).  Applicants should have an area of specialization in history of philosophy.  The program is seeking someone who can cover the rationalists, Kant, Hegel, and German idealism.  Applicants should have an area of competence in Continental philosophy. Applicants must be able to develop and deliver asynchronous online courses in support of our online degree program.  The successful candidate will be both a dynamic and inspiring educator, as well as an active and collegial full partner in the life of our small but active BA program.  This position is responsible for 12 academic units per semester (4/4). Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in Philosophy as needed, delivered both face-to-face and online.  As a member of a small BA program, each faculty member must be able to teach general education courses, courses in the history of philosophy, or other courses that fall outside their AOS.  Other responsibilities include serving as director for majors taking their capstone course, participating in the juried oral defenses of our majors each semester, and supporting the administrative functions of the unit.  Additional service responsibilities may include participation on division, department, school, college and/or university committees. Application materials should be submitted via the University's careers portal, Attention: Dr. Robert Stufflebeam.  A complete application must include: Letter of interest in the position, noting achievements in publishing, teaching, and/or service CV that includes the names and contact information for three references representative sample of research syllabi of philosophy courses taught and; a one-page statement on teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness The anticipated start date for the individual hired will be January 2027. All of the required materials must be received for an application to be considered complete. The deadline for applying is September 1, 2026 and the review will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all required materials should be submitted in the University's application portal by 11:59 PM on August 31, 2026 . Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Philosophy Evidence of teaching excellence at the University level Applicants should have an AOS in history of philosophy and an AOC in Continental philosophy. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrable expertise in curriculum development and delivery of asynchronous online courses. Competence to teach courses in each of the four performance areas of History of Philosophy, Logic, Ethics, and Metaphysics/Epistemology. Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date This position will remain open until filled. Note to Applicant: Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions at LSU New Orleans may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks. LSU New Orleans seeks to recruit a highly productive workforce and will provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and prospective employees. Employment decisions shall be based strictly on merit and without regard to religious or political beliefs, sex, race, or any other non-merit factor."
